    {
      "type": "callout",
      "tone": "warning",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The movable \"dim\" shape most players grab — and most chord apps draw — is a different chord: the four-note diminished seventh, symmetrical and built to slide. This pathway teaches the three-note triad instead, which is a quieter chord and one note smaller."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "One more place this chord turns up: walking the bass up a semitone at a time, "
        },
        {
          "text": "C",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " → "
        },
        {
          "text": "C#dim",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " → "
        },
        {
          "text": "Dm",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
